6
00:00:21.310 --> 00:00:21.790
Eisenberg.

7
00:00:21.970 --> 00:00:23.290
It's an epic episode.

8
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:28.730
And we also discussed more about the dinner party episode in our Office Lady 6.0 episode,

9
00:00:28.990 --> 00:00:30.450
Dinner Party Horror Stories.

10
00:00:31.010 --> 00:00:35.730
I was a little stumped as to what we might be able to add to the discussion in this second

11
00:00:35.730 --> 00:00:36.130
drink.

12
00:00:36.370 --> 00:00:41.570
But then I thought, why don't we read more of the fan letters from our submissions from

13
00:00:41.570 --> 00:00:42.850
Dinner Party Horror Stories?

14
00:00:43.170 --> 00:00:44.550
Yes, there were so many good ones.

15
00:00:44.610 --> 00:00:49.250
If you remember, we asked you all to send in your own Dinner Party Horror Stories, and you

16
00:00:49.250 --> 00:00:50.450
guys really delivered.

17
00:00:50.810 --> 00:00:53.450
I'm going to start us off with one from Becca J.

18
00:00:53.830 --> 00:00:54.390
in Tennessee.

19
00:00:54.830 --> 00:00:55.050
Okay.

20
00:00:55.310 --> 00:01:00.410
Becca says, when applying for medical residencies, it's common to have a dinner with current

21
00:01:00.410 --> 00:01:00.990
residents.

22
00:01:01.690 --> 00:01:05.950
This way, everyone gets a sense of the culture, and if you like them, and vice versa.

23
00:01:06.450 --> 00:01:09.950
Like many of the group, I ordered a glass of wine.

24
00:01:10.510 --> 00:01:15.610
Then I quoted Michael Scott and said I was getting an oaky afterbirth.

25
00:01:15.610 --> 00:01:20.310
Unfortunately, my dinner companions were not familiar with the U.S.

26
00:01:20.450 --> 00:01:21.990
office, including an

27
00:01:21.990 --> 00:01:25.930
Aussie who complained about the show after I explained my weird phrase.

28
00:01:26.450 --> 00:01:31.210
Ultimately, I matched with that program, and I made great friends, and I introduced the

29
00:01:31.210 --> 00:01:33.010
office to many residents.

30
00:01:33.010 --> 00:01:40.470
I mean, could you imagine the crickets if you said your wine had an oaky afterbirth to people

31
00:01:40.470 --> 00:01:43.530
who didn't get the inside joke, the office reference?

32
00:01:43.730 --> 00:01:46.170
I mean, what if this is a room full of residents?

33
00:01:46.190 --> 00:01:49.930
What if some of them are like OBGYNs, and they're like, what is happening?

34
00:01:50.950 --> 00:01:57.430
Oh, well, I liked this one from Madeline Oh, who said, one time, my husband and I were invited

35
00:01:57.430 --> 00:01:58.910
to our neighbor's house for dinner.

36
00:01:59.170 --> 00:02:05.730
She is single and mid-60s, and she had invited us and a few other neighbors our age to come.

37
00:02:06.190 --> 00:02:09.590
She provided all the food, had the best dishes out.

38
00:02:09.750 --> 00:02:11.970
It was a very fancy and proper occasion.

39
00:02:12.170 --> 00:02:16.150
Everyone was chatting quietly while we were just finishing our dinner in her dining room,

40
00:02:16.150 --> 00:02:17.530
and there was a knock.

41
00:02:17.710 --> 00:02:21.030
She said, oh, the entertainment is here.

42
00:02:21.430 --> 00:02:22.970
It was a clown.

43
00:02:23.190 --> 00:02:26.970
She had hired a clown to come entertain us millennials.

44
00:02:27.430 --> 00:02:31.030
The cringe for me right now is like, I can barely handle it.

45
00:02:32.630 --> 00:02:38.210
Madeline said, we were all very weirded out, but we sat politely in the living room while

46
00:02:38.210 --> 00:02:42.970
the clown gave us a performance clearly made for a fourth grader's birthday party.

47
00:02:43.130 --> 00:02:43.750
Oh, my gosh.

48
00:02:44.030 --> 00:02:45.930
Eventually, the clown left.

49
00:02:46.590 --> 00:02:50.210
Needless to say, we never had another dinner party with her.

50
00:02:50.670 --> 00:02:53.310
Oh, there's so much about this.

51
00:02:53.490 --> 00:02:54.490
There's so much about this.

52
00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:57.390
First of all, the clown's just doing his or her job.

53
00:02:57.530 --> 00:02:57.910
Right.

54
00:02:57.910 --> 00:02:58.710
That's what they do.

55
00:02:58.930 --> 00:03:01.650
They do clown parties for fourth graders.

56
00:03:01.990 --> 00:03:02.310
Yes.

57
00:03:02.550 --> 00:03:04.370
So imagine the clown guy.

58
00:03:04.610 --> 00:03:06.830
Like, you have a real choice in this moment.

59
00:03:07.210 --> 00:03:10.150
Do I go so hard and fully commit?

60
00:03:10.410 --> 00:03:10.610
Right.

61
00:03:11.070 --> 00:03:16.030
Or do I back off a little because I realize maybe I'm not the clown they wanted to hire?

62
00:03:16.150 --> 00:03:18.350
Or am I like, fuck you guys.

63
00:03:18.350 --> 00:03:19.610
Are you pranking me?

64
00:03:19.930 --> 00:03:24.070
Here's the thing I know about clowns is that they take clowning very seriously.

65
00:03:24.350 --> 00:03:25.850
I mean, there's like clown colleges.

66
00:03:26.170 --> 00:03:26.650
Oh, I know.

67
00:03:26.650 --> 00:03:31.650
So I have to imagine that this clown just committed.

68
00:03:32.330 --> 00:03:32.490
Yeah.

69
00:03:33.230 --> 00:03:34.870
I would go so hard.

70
00:03:35.170 --> 00:03:35.570
Yeah.

71
00:03:35.770 --> 00:03:40.450
I feel bad for this woman because it sounds like this dinner party started out nice.

72
00:03:40.530 --> 00:03:42.310
She got out her fancy dishes.

73
00:03:42.310 --> 00:03:44.010
She provided all the food.

74
00:03:44.550 --> 00:03:45.530
Something happened.

75
00:03:45.530 --> 00:03:47.090
What was the misstep here?

76
00:03:47.290 --> 00:03:48.230
What was the clown?

77
00:03:48.410 --> 00:03:49.010
Well, I know.

78
00:03:49.130 --> 00:03:50.290
But how did we get there?

79
00:03:50.410 --> 00:03:51.030
I don't know.

80
00:03:52.310 --> 00:03:53.550
What's our train of thought?

81
00:03:53.770 --> 00:03:55.890
This whole thing with this clown, like, do they commit?

82
00:03:55.970 --> 00:03:56.810
Do they not commit?

83
00:03:57.130 --> 00:03:57.470
Right.

84
00:03:57.610 --> 00:03:59.830
It's making me think of this interview.

85
00:03:59.970 --> 00:04:01.670
I just saw Jack Black do on Seth Meyers.

86
00:04:01.870 --> 00:04:03.450
Well, I'll let him explain it.

87
00:04:03.570 --> 00:04:06.810
But Jack Black was in an SNL sketch that bombed.

88
00:04:06.810 --> 00:04:09.750
But he didn't take his foot off the gas.

89
00:04:10.050 --> 00:04:10.590
He juSt.

90
00:04:10.990 --> 00:04:11.650
He went.

91
00:04:11.830 --> 00:04:12.730
