01:05:46.500 --> 01:05:47.620
She's like, is there more wine?

1213
01:05:47.840 --> 01:05:48.840
And Jan's like, no, no, no.

1214
01:05:48.900 --> 01:05:49.280
I'll get it.

1215
01:05:49.280 --> 01:05:50.760
No, actually, let's have some girl time.

1216
01:05:51.180 --> 01:05:51.900
Angela, come on.

1217
01:05:52.160 --> 01:05:53.840
And she takes them into the kitchen.

1218
01:05:54.120 --> 01:05:58.280
Well, Jenna, there were a few scenes that we filmed, us three gals, in this kitchen.

1219
01:05:58.560 --> 01:06:00.320
Only one made it into the episode.

1220
01:06:00.320 --> 01:06:02.220
But there is another one.

1221
01:06:02.220 --> 01:06:03.300
And it's great.

1222
01:06:03.620 --> 01:06:04.700
Sam, can you play it?

1223
01:06:06.120 --> 01:06:10.780
So this girl that I basically grew up with becomes Miss West Virginia.

1224
01:06:11.060 --> 01:06:13.640
And then suddenly, all the boys start paying attention to me.

1225
01:06:14.360 --> 01:06:19.780
And it was funny because, you know, I never even considered myself beautiful until people

1226
01:06:19.780 --> 01:06:21.160
started pointing it out to me.

1227
01:06:21.680 --> 01:06:26.440
You know, Jan, wow, you are so much more beautiful than Miss West Virginia.

1228
01:06:27.540 --> 01:06:32.420
Oh, so that is why I, um, wait, Pam, what was your, what was your question?

1229
01:06:32.620 --> 01:06:33.420
Where did you grow up?

1230
01:06:35.300 --> 01:06:35.800
Incredible.

1231
01:06:36.520 --> 01:06:37.740
Isn't it so good?

1232
01:06:38.080 --> 01:06:38.600
Yeah.

1233
01:06:38.920 --> 01:06:41.500
She just goes off about Miss West Virginia.

1234
01:06:41.500 --> 01:06:44.580
And we're just sitting there in silence as she's chopping things.

1235
01:06:44.580 --> 01:06:46.680
She clearly hates this woman.

1236
01:06:47.160 --> 01:06:49.860
My question was, where did you grow up?

1237
01:06:50.120 --> 01:06:50.320
Yeah.

1238
01:06:50.720 --> 01:06:55.700
And in the kitchen scene, you'll notice I'm standing behind a little ledge by the counter.

1239
01:06:55.780 --> 01:07:00.200
And I remember Paul Feig and I were so excited that there was a ledge in the kitchen.

1240
01:07:00.420 --> 01:07:01.700
They didn't have to build that.

1241
01:07:01.840 --> 01:07:05.060
And I fit perfectly tucked into it so we could hide my belly.

1242
01:07:05.280 --> 01:07:10.200
Well, while the ladies are having their time in the kitchen, Michael gives the guys a tour

1243
01:07:10.200 --> 01:07:10.880
of the garage.

1244
01:07:11.360 --> 01:07:16.660
He also uses this time to try to get them to invest in Serenity by Jan.

1245
01:07:16.980 --> 01:07:17.600
And he's in.

1246
01:07:17.940 --> 01:07:20.280
You don't need to say more than a sentence to him.

1247
01:07:20.680 --> 01:07:25.400
This is my daughter's favorite line in the whole episode is when he goes, thought about

1248
01:07:25.400 --> 01:07:25.620
it.

1249
01:07:25.820 --> 01:07:26.220
I'm in.

1250
01:07:26.860 --> 01:07:27.060
Yeah.

1251
01:07:27.060 --> 01:07:32.420
And Michael's like, do you want to invest $10,000 into this candle business?

1252
01:07:32.900 --> 01:07:33.640
Think about it.

1253
01:07:33.740 --> 01:07:34.780
Thought about it.

1254
01:07:34.900 --> 01:07:35.360
I'm in.

1255
01:07:36.060 --> 01:07:41.920
Well, when we asked Ed about his memories from shooting The Dinner Party, he talked about

1256
01:07:41.920 --> 01:07:44.540
the first time he saw this garage.

1257
01:07:45.180 --> 01:07:46.580
Sam, can you play that clip?

1258
01:07:47.880 --> 01:07:51.420
At some point while we were shooting, I stepped off the set.

1259
01:07:51.560 --> 01:07:55.320
I think I was probably just going to get a snack or something at craft service.

1260
01:07:55.520 --> 01:07:58.780
And I walked through the garage of the condo where we were shooting.

1261
01:07:59.040 --> 01:08:02.120
And the garage was also a location in the episode.

1262
01:08:02.320 --> 01:08:04.500
They had done all the set decoration for the garage.

1263
01:08:04.500 --> 01:08:10.640
And I noticed this amazing detail in there, which is that all of the items in Michael Scott's

1264
01:08:10.640 --> 01:08:16.860
garage were things that he had bought from infomercials, like late night infomercials.

1265
01:08:16.980 --> 01:08:20.560
And this was just like a background joke in the show.

1266
01:08:20.780 --> 01:08:25.700
Like, I remember seeing like a Bowflex and like a meat dehydrator, like all this random

1267
01:08:25.700 --> 01:08:26.100
stuff.

1268
01:08:26.100 --> 01:08:31.940
And it just made me laugh so hard and was such a reminder of how incredible The Office team

1269
01:08:31.940 --> 01:08:37.540
was, everyone at every level from production design, set decoration, all those details,

1270
01:08:37.780 --> 01:08:42.560
all of those people that worked on the show were so creative and contributing to the comedy

1271
01:08:42.560 --> 01:08:46.180
of that show in very big and very small ways.

1272
01:08:46.180 --> 01:08:48.480
And it all made such a difference.

1273
01:08:48.860 --> 01:08:51.480
Anyway, that's one of my favorite details about that episode.

1274
01:08:52.860 --> 01:08:55.080
Angela, I looked it up.

1275
01:08:55.610 --> 01:08:59.720
So currently a Bowflex system starts around $1,500.

1276
01:08:59.720 --> 01:09:05.620
But Michael had both a Bowflex and a Soloflex.

1277
01:09:05.920 --> 01:09:09.260
And a Soloflex is like $2,400.

1278
01:09:10.180 --> 01:09:17.580
And then like Ed said, like meat dehydrator, just any as seen on TV item was shoved into

1279
01:09:17.580 --> 01:09:18.300
the space.

1280
01:09:18.480 --> 01:09:20.380
And really pricey stuff.

1281
01:09:20.540 --> 01:09:24.760
There's two boxes of La Cousette, like Dutch ovens.

1282
01:09:24.900 --> 01:09:26.560
Those are so expensive.

1283
01:09:27.120 --> 01:09:28.820
They're like at Williams-Sonoma.

1284
01:09:28.820 --> 01:09:28.880
Yeah.

1285
01:09:29.040 --> 01:09:33.380
And it just kind of is that reminder of when Oscar sat down with him and said, what are

1286
01:09:33.380 --> 01:09:33.920
you buying?

1287
01:09:34.060 --> 01:09:35.640
What are you spending your money on?

1288
01:09:36.080 --> 01:09:42.360
And I don't know if you noticed, but there's also just boxes labeled Michael's stuff.

1289
01:09:42.740 --> 01:09:42.900
Yeah.

1290
01:09:43.300 --> 01:09:48.920
So clearly Jan went through and just boxed up a bunch of his stuff and it's out there

1291
01:09:48.920 --> 01:09:49.920
living in the garage.

1292
01:09:50.060 --> 01:09:50.900
So sad.

1293
01:09:50.900 --> 01:09:51.520
Oh yeah.

1294
01:09:51.680 --> 01:09:55.100
You know, the two chairs by that fireplace were those two hand seats.

1295
01:09:56.220 --> 01:09:57.140
That's right.

1296
01:09:57.380 --> 01:09:59.880
But those aren't in the living room anymore.

1297
01:10:00.580 --> 01:10:02.460
Lady, I think we should take a break.

1298
01:10:02.740 --> 01:10:05.600
We still have so much more to talk about.

1299
01:10:05.900 --> 01:10:06.680
Oh my gosh.

1300
01:10:06.900 --> 01:10:09.760
Dwight and the babysitter haven't even showed up yet.

1301
01:10:09.980 --> 01:10:12.800
Well, we will get to that right after this break.

1302
01:10:23.690 --> 01:10:24.630
Ding dong.

1303
01:10:26.940 --> 01:10:29.160
Oh, there's two more guests.

1304
01:10:29.600 --> 01:10:30.880
Jan is confused.

1305
01:10:31.300 --> 01:10:32.800
Her whole dinner party is here.

1306
01:10:33.060 --> 01:10:34.280
Michael is not.

1307
01:10:34.500 --> 01:10:35.980
He knows who's at the door.

1308
01:10:36.240 --> 01:10:42.480
It's Dwight and Melvina, his older babysitter from when he was a child.

1309
01:10:42.860 --> 01:10:43.880
Oh, and don't worry.

1310
01:10:44.100 --> 01:10:47.340
They've brought two wine glasses and a cooler of food.

1311
01:10:47.460 --> 01:10:47.840
Yeah.

1312
01:10:48.020 --> 01:10:50.320
Since they're unexpected, they've got it covered.

1313
01:10:50.540 --> 01:10:50.960
Don't worry.

1314
01:10:51.240 --> 01:10:52.620
And two lawn chairs.

1315
01:10:53.260 --> 01:10:55.260
So they have a place to sit.

1316
01:10:55.520 --> 01:10:58.500
The wine glasses are the biggest ones you'll ever see.

1317
01:10:58.860 --> 01:10:59.920
Yes, they are.

1318
01:11:00.320 --> 01:11:01.880
This sets off an argument.

1319
01:11:02.360 --> 01:11:07.000
Jan wants Michael to send them away, but Michael stands his ground.

1320
01:11:07.420 --> 01:11:07.980
Yeah.

1321
01:11:08.180 --> 01:11:12.380
Michael's like, listen, you said he couldn't come because he didn't have a plus

1322
01:11:12.380 --> 01:11:15.160
one or we didn't have enough wine glasses.

1323
01:11:15.300 --> 01:11:17.600
Well, he brought the wine glasses and he brought another human.

1324
01:11:17.860 --> 01:11:18.500
I know.

1325
01:11:18.640 --> 01:11:19.220
I love that.

1326
01:11:19.400 --> 01:11:20.660
He's brought a person.

1327
01:11:20.800 --> 01:11:21.380
A person.

1328
01:11:21.840 --> 01:11:22.980
So here we go.

1329
01:11:23.280 --> 01:11:26.220
And Jan is like, fine, have it your way.

1330
01:11:26.380 --> 01:11:28.600
And Michael's like, have it my way.

1331
01:11:28.720 --> 01:11:31.520
When do things ever go my way?

1332
01:11:31.760 --> 01:11:32.240
Yeah.

1333
01:11:32.440 --> 01:11:36.200
When he wanted to see Stump and she wanted to see Wicked, what did they see?

1334
01:11:36.560 --> 01:11:37.000
Wicked.

1335
01:11:37.380 --> 01:11:41.520
When she said she wasn't ready to have children, what did Michael do?

1336
01:11:41.520 --> 01:11:42.680
He had a vasectomy.

1337
01:11:42.860 --> 01:11:44.700
Then she decided, I want kids.

1338
01:11:44.860 --> 01:11:46.400
He had the vasectomy reversed.

1339
01:11:46.660 --> 01:11:48.140
But then she changed her mind again.

1340
01:11:48.140 --> 01:11:49.720
He had another vasectomy.

1341
01:11:50.020 --> 01:11:51.520
Zip, snap, zip, snap, zip, snap.

1342
01:11:52.020 --> 01:11:56.240
Do you know the physical toll that three vasectomies takes on a person?

1343
01:11:57.080 --> 01:12:01.480
Oh, all of this happens in front of all of us.

1344
01:12:01.740 --> 01:12:04.480
There is so much to unpack about this scene, guys.

1345
01:12:04.740 --> 01:12:05.740
So buckle in.

1346
01:12:05.740 --> 01:12:10.680
I mean, when we saw The Bench, we thought, it can't get weirder than The Bench.

1347
01:12:10.800 --> 01:12:14.300
And then we played Celebrity.

1348
01:12:14.560 --> 01:12:21.840
And now we're standing in the hallway of the condo yelling about vasectomies?

1349
01:12:22.020 --> 01:12:23.460
Where can it go?

1350
01:12:23.460 --> 01:12:28.480
Let's start with Dwight's date, his former babysitter, Melvina.

1351
01:12:29.040 --> 01:12:35.020
Angela, Jean told me that they thought it would be really fun to offer this role to our longtime

1352
01:12:35.020 --> 01:12:37.320
casting director, Alison Jones.

1353
01:12:37.560 --> 01:12:38.900
But she said no.

1354
01:12:39.240 --> 01:12:40.260
She refused.

1355
01:12:42.440 --> 01:12:48.040
Greg wanted the incredible Beth Grant to play the role.

1356
01:12:48.040 --> 01:12:52.460
Well, yes, Greg had worked with Beth before and knew her very well.

1357
01:12:52.700 --> 01:12:56.880
You guys might recognize her from the film No Country for Old Men.

1358
01:12:57.080 --> 01:12:58.760
I mean, she has a huge filmography.

1359
01:12:58.960 --> 01:13:01.820
But at this time, that film had just come out.

1360
01:13:02.220 --> 01:13:03.800
We reached out to Beth.

1361
01:13:04.180 --> 01:13:10.020
And she told us the story of exactly how she was cast on the show.

1362
01:13:10.020 --> 01:13:18.480
I was thrilled when I got the call to do this part and to be Rain's babysitter and girlfriend.

1363
01:13:20.500 --> 01:13:23.220
It's demented, and I love it.

1364
01:13:23.340 --> 01:13:27.980
And I had worked with Steve Carell fairly recently in Little Miss Sunshine.

1365
01:13:27.980 --> 01:13:32.020
So I was already completely in love with him and did love the show.

1366
01:13:32.160 --> 01:13:35.600
And I had worked with Greg Daniels on King of the Hill.

1367
01:13:35.780 --> 01:13:39.120
And we ran into each other during the Writers Guild strike.

1368
01:13:39.120 --> 01:13:41.760
And I think he saw me in my strike mode.

1369
01:13:41.780 --> 01:13:45.760
I guess he knew I was right to be able to be that demented woman.

1370
01:13:48.180 --> 01:13:53.340
Well, then Beth shares with us what it was like to do the scene at the front door.

1371
01:13:53.480 --> 01:13:55.480
She's holding a cooler the whole time.

1372
01:13:55.600 --> 01:13:56.940
This is all happening.

1373
01:13:57.100 --> 01:13:59.520
It's her first scene of the episode.

1374
01:13:59.820 --> 01:14:01.080
Here's what she had to say.

1375
01:14:01.580 --> 01:14:06.400
Coming to the door to that dinner party was so thrilling for me.

1376
01:14:06.400 --> 01:14:08.780
It was so hard not to laugh.

1377
01:14:09.120 --> 01:14:12.580
I felt that since I knew Steve, he was out to get me.

1378
01:14:12.740 --> 01:14:13.960
He wanted me to break.

1379
01:14:13.960 --> 01:14:21.420
And here I was, a guest star, nervous with all you regulars, you fabulous comedians, you brilliant comic minds.

1380
01:14:21.740 --> 01:14:24.600
And here I am, the guest star with Rain.

1381
01:14:24.920 --> 01:14:28.720
And opening the door is Steve Carell, just going for it.

1382
01:14:28.720 --> 01:14:34.260
And I started this riff and improvising to the point that I was determined not to laugh.

1383
01:14:34.260 --> 01:14:37.120
So I started almost grunting and crying.

1384
01:14:39.660 --> 01:14:44.220
I don't know if you can hear it in the episode, but, and tears in my eyes.

1385
01:14:44.300 --> 01:14:45.440
And he said, oh, great.

1386
01:14:45.620 --> 01:14:47.000
Now she's crying or something.

1387
01:14:47.100 --> 01:14:48.580
And I leaned over.

1388
01:14:48.740 --> 01:14:51.860
I was holding that cooler, you know, bringing our own food.

1389
01:14:52.260 --> 01:14:55.220
Since we weren't invited, holding that cooler.

1390
01:14:55.220 --> 01:14:58.980
And I leaned over, just shaking all over and came back up.

1391
01:14:59.080 --> 01:15:01.620
And somehow I think I managed not to break.

1392
01:15:01.760 --> 01:15:06.740
But that was the only time I managed not to break because you guys were just so hilarious.

1393
01:15:07.360 --> 01:15:13.360
Jenna, we should share with everyone what line Steve improvised that sent us all to the floor.

1394
01:15:13.940 --> 01:15:14.300
Yes.

1395
01:15:14.900 --> 01:15:19.140
Guys, Steve improvised the line, snip, snap, snip, snap.

1396
01:15:19.380 --> 01:15:23.900
You have no idea the physical toll three vasectomies has on a person.

1397
01:15:24.260 --> 01:15:31.140
I mean, you try not laughing with Steve Carell in front of you improvising stuff like that.

1398
01:15:31.260 --> 01:15:32.640
We were all a goner.

1399
01:15:32.640 --> 01:15:38.840
Well, it's interesting because Paul Feig sent in an audio clip about this, and I'll let him explain it.

1400
01:15:38.940 --> 01:15:42.220
But there's a reason why Steve improvised that line.

1401
01:15:42.540 --> 01:15:43.180
Here you go.

1402
01:15:43.800 --> 01:15:46.920
There's so many great things to think about and remember from this episode.

1403
01:15:47.100 --> 01:15:53.700
But the one that makes me just realize how genius Steve Carell is, in case anybody didn't realize that already,

1404
01:15:54.660 --> 01:16:00.760
is when the whole snip, snap run was, it was a pretty dramatic scene of them,

1405
01:16:01.200 --> 01:16:03.640
like talking about having kids and all this.

1406
01:16:03.760 --> 01:16:05.720
And so we did several takes of it.

1407
01:16:05.820 --> 01:16:07.440
It was really good, but it was very dramatic.

1408
01:16:07.640 --> 01:16:09.440
And I remember kind of saying to Steve,

1409
01:16:10.220 --> 01:16:12.880
maybe let's do a take or just kind of find a little more humor in it.

1410
01:16:12.940 --> 01:16:15.480
I know it's kind of hard because it's kind of a serious subject.

1411
01:16:15.640 --> 01:16:16.820
And he's like, oh, okay, yeah, I get it.

1412
01:16:16.880 --> 01:16:17.080
I get it.

1413
01:16:17.140 --> 01:16:20.360
And that's when he did it, went off on the whole snip, snap, snip, snap,

1414
01:16:20.920 --> 01:16:21.840
which is just brilliant.

1415
01:16:22.000 --> 01:16:26.180
I mean, that scene is so funny because it's so heartbreaking and cringy, but also hilarious.

1416
01:16:26.780 --> 01:16:28.480
I remember that, Angela.

1417
01:16:28.720 --> 01:16:33.780
I remember doing takes and takes of that scene where they were just going back and forth.

1418
01:16:33.980 --> 01:16:39.440
And you could just see the pain and Michael that he wasn't a father and that Jan had been

1419
01:16:39.440 --> 01:16:40.940
so manipulative of him.

1420
01:16:41.060 --> 01:16:42.660
And it was like a drama.

1421
01:16:42.900 --> 01:16:45.340
And then Paul came over and talked to Steve.

1422
01:16:45.720 --> 01:16:49.380
And they were like, how can we make this a comedy again?

1423
01:16:49.740 --> 01:16:55.300
How can we keep the dark elements of this scene but not let it get too heavy?

1424
01:16:56.180 --> 01:16:57.180
Brilliant Steve Carell.

1425
01:16:57.380 --> 01:16:59.740
Yeah, he so saves the moment.

1426
01:16:59.740 --> 01:17:00.820
And it's hilarious.

1427
01:17:01.120 --> 01:17:02.020
I mean, you're cringing.

1428
01:17:02.020 --> 01:17:02.860
It's horrible.

1429
01:17:03.120 --> 01:17:03.460
It's...

1430
01:17:03.460 --> 01:17:05.680
But he makes it funny.

1431
01:17:06.300 --> 01:17:06.860
Yeah.

1432
01:17:07.140 --> 01:17:09.740
Well, now, guys, we're going to sit down at the table.

1433
01:17:10.000 --> 01:17:11.640
I guess dinner is ready.

1434
01:17:12.140 --> 01:17:13.000
Near ready.

1435
01:17:13.260 --> 01:17:13.740
Finally.

1436
01:17:14.340 --> 01:17:16.000
Can I point something out?

1437
01:17:16.280 --> 01:17:16.500
Yeah.

1438
01:17:16.740 --> 01:17:21.280
If you look at the table, we all have wine glasses, right?

1439
01:17:21.500 --> 01:17:21.780
Mm-hmm.

1440
01:17:21.780 --> 01:17:27.440
We also all have water glasses, which are wine glasses.

1441
01:17:28.040 --> 01:17:35.780
So clearly, Jan had more than six wine glasses because she is using them for water as well.

1442
01:17:35.920 --> 01:17:40.180
She just didn't want Dwight to come, you guys, to her fancy party.

1443
01:17:40.200 --> 01:17:42.380
He did not make the liSt.

1444
01:17:42.780 --> 01:17:45.600
Well, Dwight has started eating.

1445
01:17:45.940 --> 01:17:47.220
I mean, they brought their own food.

1446
01:17:47.380 --> 01:17:48.660
They're wasting no time.

1447
01:17:49.220 --> 01:17:50.420
They're the only ones eating.

1448
01:17:51.060 --> 01:17:53.840
Jan is still upset over what happened at the door.

1449
01:17:54.140 --> 01:17:56.320
She's so upset, she has to excuse herself.

1450
01:17:56.440 --> 01:17:57.340
She goes to the kitchen.

1451
01:17:57.680 --> 01:17:57.880
Yeah.

1452
01:17:58.120 --> 01:18:02.100
I mean, the last thing she said before she sat at that dining table was,

1453
01:18:02.240 --> 01:18:03.220
I hate my life.

1454
01:18:03.840 --> 01:18:04.200
Yeah.

1455
01:18:04.480 --> 01:18:05.920
She's not in a good place.

1456
01:18:06.440 --> 01:18:09.420
Jenna, there's a deleted scene that is so fantastic,

1457
01:18:09.420 --> 01:18:12.200
where you kind of whisper to Michael,

1458
01:18:12.580 --> 01:18:13.300
go to Jan.

1459
01:18:13.560 --> 01:18:14.880
Go comfort her.

1460
01:18:15.100 --> 01:18:17.660
You kind of do this little motion, like, go say something.

1461
01:18:17.660 --> 01:18:20.420
So he gets up, and he walks over to her.

1462
01:18:20.820 --> 01:18:25.620
Again, he's comforting her, but we're all witness to it.

1463
01:18:26.300 --> 01:18:29.560
And it's so clumsy and awkward.

1464
01:18:30.160 --> 01:18:32.660
And Sam, can you play the first part of that?

1465
01:18:33.660 --> 01:18:35.500
Hey, no, no, no.

1466
01:18:35.600 --> 01:18:36.160
Don't be sad.

1467
01:18:36.600 --> 01:18:37.400
Don't be sad.

1468
01:18:38.500 --> 01:18:40.900
Look, I care about you, and I support you.

1469
01:18:44.300 --> 01:18:47.560
And you are smart and beautiful.

1470
01:18:49.680 --> 01:18:54.900
And you have beautiful bosoms, and you can't even tell they're fake unless you're naked.

1471
01:18:56.640 --> 01:19:02.860
And I believe that with my support and your constant calls to Dr. Perry on my phone plan,

1472
01:19:02.860 --> 01:19:08.340
which is a little bit of a strain, because I only have 20 anytime minutes a month.

1473
01:19:09.160 --> 01:19:11.240
Every minute after that is 75 cents.

1474
01:19:12.240 --> 01:19:12.720
Oh.

1475
01:19:13.680 --> 01:19:15.920
You should look at some other plans.

1476
01:19:16.280 --> 01:19:16.920
Oh, okay.

1477
01:19:17.220 --> 01:19:18.140
Thanks, weirdo.

1478
01:19:18.280 --> 01:19:19.000
But you know what?

1479
01:19:19.180 --> 01:19:21.480
I'm month to month because I don't want a two-year commitment.

1480
01:19:23.080 --> 01:19:27.760
I remember when he turned to Beth and goes, oh, thanks, weirdo.

1481
01:19:28.060 --> 01:19:29.720
We all lost it.

1482
01:19:30.380 --> 01:19:30.500
Yeah.

1483
01:19:31.220 --> 01:19:33.920
Gene said that's one of his favorite lines that got cut.

1484
01:19:34.180 --> 01:19:35.060
Oh, really?

1485
01:19:35.520 --> 01:19:35.920
Mm-hmm.

1486
01:19:36.220 --> 01:19:37.600
He loves that moment.

1487
01:19:38.220 --> 01:19:42.680
Michael continues to try to comfort Jan, and it doesn't get any better,

1488
01:19:42.840 --> 01:19:46.900
but it really paints a picture of how he feels about his home life with her.

1489
01:19:48.000 --> 01:19:49.340
What were you saying to Jan?

1490
01:19:49.340 --> 01:19:56.040
Honey, nobody in the complex likes you, but you have made this place look great.

1491
01:19:56.600 --> 01:19:58.160
It's like a museum.

1492
01:19:58.460 --> 01:19:58.700
Yeah.

1493
01:19:59.580 --> 01:20:08.980
You can't touch anything, which is a really strange way to feel in the place that you live.

1494
01:20:10.100 --> 01:20:13.520
You have made this home a house.

1495
01:20:15.080 --> 01:20:19.440
It's just what Paul Feig said about their design of the house.

1496
01:20:19.500 --> 01:20:20.100
Yes.

1497
01:20:20.280 --> 01:20:21.120
Like a museum.

1498
01:20:21.440 --> 01:20:24.820
You have made this warm, cozy home a house.

1499
01:20:26.560 --> 01:20:27.700
Oh, Michael.

1500
01:20:27.920 --> 01:20:33.080
I think they were right to leave those out because otherwise I think we might have felt

1501
01:20:33.080 --> 01:20:38.120
too badly for Jan when Michael is about to do what he's about to do.

1502
01:20:38.120 --> 01:20:43.880
But before we get there, Angela, I have to talk about this moment when Dwight offers you

1503
01:20:43.880 --> 01:20:47.760
some of his beet salad and you respond by saying,

1504
01:20:47.980 --> 01:20:52.660
the thought of popping one of his beets into your mouth makes you want to vomit.

1505
01:20:53.460 --> 01:20:56.860
Because I remember something else that was happening during this scene.

1506
01:20:56.940 --> 01:20:57.900
Will you share it with us?

1507
01:20:57.900 --> 01:21:04.300
Yeah, it was actually really hard for me to focus in this scene and say my dialogue because

1508
01:21:04.300 --> 01:21:09.640
Jenna, my daughter in my belly, just decided in that moment she was going to run a full

1509
01:21:09.640 --> 01:21:10.060
marathon.

1510
01:21:10.500 --> 01:21:13.900
She was like, digging, digging, digging, digging, digging, digging, kicking so much.

1511
01:21:14.060 --> 01:21:14.600
I don't know.

1512
01:21:14.700 --> 01:21:16.920
Maybe it's the sound of Rainn Wilson's voice.

1513
01:21:17.660 --> 01:21:22.820
Maybe Rainn's voice awoken my child in my womb and she was ready to fight.

1514
01:21:22.820 --> 01:21:29.480
But it was so surreal to me to be thinking about the timing of the scene and everyone's

1515
01:21:29.480 --> 01:21:32.540
dialogue and when I was supposed to come in and trying not to laugh.

1516
01:21:32.740 --> 01:21:37.280
In the meantime, having this like wrestling match happening in my belly.

1517
01:21:37.560 --> 01:21:40.380
I think there are a lot of women who can relate to that, Angela.

1518
01:21:40.620 --> 01:21:44.820
I have a friend who is a lawyer and she was very, very pregnant and she was having to take

1519
01:21:44.820 --> 01:21:45.460
a deposition.

1520
01:21:45.740 --> 01:21:50.260
And she told me at the end of the day, she was like, I could barely focus on what I was

1521
01:21:50.260 --> 01:21:58.740
doing because I was having to give very carefully worded questions and comments because it was

1522
01:21:58.740 --> 01:21:59.840
all going on the record.

1523
01:22:00.020 --> 01:22:02.860
But all the while, her kid in her belly was just tossing and turning.

1524
01:22:03.320 --> 01:22:05.400
Yeah, so much so.

1525
01:22:05.560 --> 01:22:08.920
And I have shared this story before and it's one of my favorite memories.

1526
01:22:09.240 --> 01:22:13.660
While the scene was going on, I'm talking, everyone is saying their lines and there's

1527
01:22:13.660 --> 01:22:22.120
the rapid cadence of the dialogue, I, off camera, grabbed Ed's hand and under the table, put it

1528
01:22:22.120 --> 01:22:29.280
on my belly and he turned to me with his eyes wide and all of a sudden he wasn't Andy, he

1529
01:22:29.280 --> 01:22:39.370
was Ed and he mouthed to me, oh my, to know and to witness like what I was like going through

1530
01:22:39.370 --> 01:22:39.990
in the moment.

1531
01:22:40.250 --> 01:22:42.350
And it's such a special memory to me.

1532
01:22:42.350 --> 01:22:47.390
And when I rewatched the episode with my daughter, I said, Isabel, you were running a

1533
01:22:47.390 --> 01:22:49.210
marathon in mommy's belly right now.

1534
01:22:49.330 --> 01:22:50.210
And she was like, what?

1535
01:22:50.790 --> 01:22:52.230
It's so special to me.

1536
01:22:52.710 --> 01:22:54.630
Guys, women are warriors.

1537
01:22:55.170 --> 01:23:00.230
We go to work and we focus on our work as if we don't have that going on.

1538
01:23:00.610 --> 01:23:06.330
Try to imagine how I could put it to a man like, okay, you're trying to give the most important

1539
01:23:06.330 --> 01:23:10.530
presentation of your life and imagine a puppy is jumping at your leg the whole time.

1540
01:23:10.530 --> 01:23:13.570
Like, just the most distracting thing.

1541
01:23:13.910 --> 01:23:17.650
Jumping at your leg, but it's inside you, which is even weirder.

1542
01:23:18.150 --> 01:23:18.530
Yeah.

1543
01:23:18.810 --> 01:23:20.010
It's like the alien.

1544
01:23:20.010 --> 01:23:20.910
What is happening?

1545
01:23:21.370 --> 01:23:22.410
Women are warriors.

1546
01:23:22.930 --> 01:23:23.930
Way to go, Ange.

1547
01:23:24.370 --> 01:23:28.650
Beth Grant also shared her memories about shooting this dinner table scene.

1548
01:23:28.810 --> 01:23:29.970
Let's have a listen.

1549
01:23:30.450 --> 01:23:33.990
Sitting at that table and, you know, sucking on those beets.

1550
01:23:34.150 --> 01:23:36.990
The reason I was sucking on those beets was to keep from laughing.

1551
01:23:36.990 --> 01:23:42.930
And Rain's over there eating and going, mm, mm, mm, mm, mm, mm.

1552
01:23:43.050 --> 01:23:47.110
There's so much subtle humor in this episode.

1553
01:23:47.110 --> 01:23:50.950
And then, of course, the demented relationship that they have.

1554
01:23:51.090 --> 01:23:52.690
I love you all so much.

1555
01:23:52.750 --> 01:23:57.790
I'm so honored to be part of this very popular and respected episode.

1556
01:23:57.970 --> 01:24:02.910
Each of you doing such beautiful, subtle, hilarious comedy.

1557
01:24:02.910 --> 01:24:06.210
And I was so thrilled to see that all of you broke up, too.

1558
01:24:06.350 --> 01:24:11.110
Once we got inside and we sat down at the table and someone would break and say, sorry, sorry.

1559
01:24:11.270 --> 01:24:13.310
And then someone else would break, sorry, sorry.

1560
01:24:13.490 --> 01:24:14.390
And then we'd keep going.

1561
01:24:14.690 --> 01:24:20.470
The last thing I'll say is when I came home, I said, I do not know how Paul is going to edit this.

1562
01:24:20.870 --> 01:24:22.170
It's too hilarious.

1563
01:24:22.570 --> 01:24:24.590
Every moment is a three-hour episode.

1564
01:24:24.590 --> 01:24:26.650
I don't understand how he's going to do it.

1565
01:24:26.650 --> 01:24:28.470
But by golly, you did it.

1566
01:24:28.590 --> 01:24:36.630
And it is just an honor to have been part of this amazing, and as I say again, demented episode.

1567
01:24:39.590 --> 01:24:40.950
Amazing and demented.

1568
01:24:41.990 --> 01:24:43.430
That sums it up.

1569
01:24:43.650 --> 01:24:43.790
Yeah.

1570
01:24:44.290 --> 01:24:49.890
Gene told me that he and Lee actually begged NBC to make this a supersized episode.

1571
01:24:50.170 --> 01:24:52.970
But I guess the schedule had already been set.

1572
01:24:52.970 --> 01:25:03.970
But he also told me that they did end up releasing a 29-minute producer's cut on iTunes that included a bunch of deleted scenes, including some of the ones we talked about,

1573
01:25:04.170 --> 01:25:05.630
like the granola bar scene.

1574
01:25:06.110 --> 01:25:11.370
Maybe NBC didn't supersize it because they were holding a grudge because Greg wanted it to go as is.

1575
01:25:12.010 --> 01:25:12.350
Ooh.

1576
01:25:14.190 --> 01:25:14.710
Wow.

1577
01:25:14.710 --> 01:25:16.250
I love that speculation.

1578
01:25:16.370 --> 01:25:21.050
They're like, no, you can have your weirdo episode, but it's only going to be 22 minutes.

1579
01:25:21.070 --> 01:25:22.450
We're not going to make it big.

1580
01:25:23.050 --> 01:25:24.310
That's what she said.

1581
01:25:24.530 --> 01:25:26.190
Oh, that's what she said.

1582
01:25:27.250 --> 01:25:33.810
One other little detail from this dinner party is how enormous the glasses were that Dwight was drinking from.

1583
01:25:34.070 --> 01:25:36.690
To me, they look like glasses you buy at Spencer's Gifts.

1584
01:25:36.890 --> 01:25:41.270
Remember that place in the mall where you could get, like, kind of joke-sized stuff?

1585
01:25:41.550 --> 01:25:46.450
Well, Paul really loved these glasses, and there was one detail about them he wanted to share with us.

1586
01:25:46.990 --> 01:25:53.770
One of my favorite gags in the show is when Dwight comes over with his babysitter and they're at dinner with the wine glasses.

1587
01:25:53.770 --> 01:26:00.870
I had them fill the wine all the way to the top because I figured that's what Dwight would think you would do with a big wine glass is you would fill it right to the rim.

1588
01:26:00.870 --> 01:26:05.110
So that's a little wine lover's joke for everybody.

1589
01:26:05.650 --> 01:26:07.730
You know what they look like to me, Angela?

1590
01:26:08.010 --> 01:26:14.970
They look like those wine glasses that I see a lot of moms post on Instagram about getting through their day.

1591
01:26:15.490 --> 01:26:19.570
Wine weekend with the ladies and the wine glasses like the size of your head.

1592
01:26:19.790 --> 01:26:20.230
Yes.

1593
01:26:20.530 --> 01:26:22.030
That's what they remind me of.

1594
01:26:22.250 --> 01:26:22.490
Yeah.

1595
01:26:22.810 --> 01:26:23.790
Oh, my God.

1596
01:26:23.990 --> 01:26:24.790
Lady, guess what?

1597
01:26:24.990 --> 01:26:25.290
What?

1598
01:26:25.290 --> 01:26:26.810
The food is ready.

1599
01:26:27.170 --> 01:26:29.590
The food is ready, but it might be poisoned.

1600
01:26:30.010 --> 01:26:30.850
Oh, no.

1601
01:26:31.330 --> 01:26:32.410
Oh, my gosh.

1602
01:26:32.490 --> 01:26:32.790
Yes.

1603
01:26:32.950 --> 01:26:34.290
Michael whispers to Pam.

1604
01:26:34.610 --> 01:26:38.930
He thinks that Jan has maybe been trying to poison him.

1605
01:26:39.070 --> 01:26:41.090
He can't prove it, but he thinks.

1606
01:26:41.410 --> 01:26:44.170
He just hopes she didn't do anything to the food tonight.

1607
01:26:44.530 --> 01:26:45.990
Like, what has been happening to Michael?

1608
01:26:46.110 --> 01:26:47.670
Has he been having violent diarrhea?

1609
01:26:48.170 --> 01:26:50.550
Stomach cramping after he eats with her?

1610
01:26:50.770 --> 01:26:52.830
Like, what is making him think this?

1611
01:26:53.430 --> 01:26:54.910
Pam has a talking head.

1612
01:26:55.190 --> 01:26:56.770
Poor Pam is so hungry.

1613
01:26:57.050 --> 01:27:00.450
She says she knows that Jan did not poison the food.

1614
01:27:00.690 --> 01:27:08.590
But if she were going to poison the food, wouldn't she have poisoned Pam since she is Michael's former lover?

1615
01:27:09.530 --> 01:27:12.570
And now you know Pam is not going to be able to eat.

1616
01:27:12.850 --> 01:27:14.990
You guys, Michael has soft teeth.

1617
01:27:15.410 --> 01:27:16.950
We learned that in this episode.

1618
01:27:17.430 --> 01:27:23.750
And because of his soft teeth, he has to dip his meat into his wine or probably whatever beverage is in front of him.

1619
01:27:24.010 --> 01:27:26.350
And Jan hates it.

1620
01:27:26.730 --> 01:27:28.890
This has clearly come up before.

1621
01:27:29.310 --> 01:27:30.690
And she doesn't want him to do it.

1622
01:27:30.750 --> 01:27:31.870
She's like, could you stop doing it?

1623
01:27:31.970 --> 01:27:32.790
It's disgusting.

1624
01:27:33.630 --> 01:27:36.230
Lady, can I tell you a story about a guy I dated?

1625
01:27:36.470 --> 01:27:36.930
Oh, God.

1626
01:27:36.930 --> 01:27:40.470
I was so worried you were about to tell me you dipped meat into your beverages.

1627
01:27:40.470 --> 01:27:41.670
But it's about a different.

1628
01:27:41.850 --> 01:27:42.310
It's a guy.

1629
01:27:42.850 --> 01:27:45.370
Angela, how long have you known me?

1630
01:27:45.370 --> 01:27:49.870
You thought maybe I dip my meat in beverages?

1631
01:27:50.110 --> 01:27:51.590
Well, you made a face.

1632
01:27:51.590 --> 01:27:53.050
You guys can't see her.

1633
01:27:53.150 --> 01:27:54.750
But she made a face.

1634
01:27:54.970 --> 01:28:00.470
You did the thing with your shoulders that you do, Jenna, when you're about to share something with me that you haven't shared before.

1635
01:28:00.710 --> 01:28:02.410
And so I thought, oh, my God.

1636
01:28:02.850 --> 01:28:05.370
I've eaten with her, but have I ever eaten red meat with her?

1637
01:28:05.510 --> 01:28:06.030
Oh, my God.

1638
01:28:06.630 --> 01:28:08.550
No, I eat meat normally.

1639
01:28:08.710 --> 01:28:11.370
I can't believe that's a sentence I had to say.

1640
01:28:11.570 --> 01:28:11.970
Well.

1641
01:28:12.190 --> 01:28:12.910
But I did.

1642
01:28:13.190 --> 01:28:13.630
No.

1643
01:28:13.630 --> 01:28:21.230
So what I was going to share was I dated a guy who, first of all, had to drink milk with every meal, not water.

1644
01:28:21.610 --> 01:28:25.190
He is a grown man, but he had to have a big, tall glass of milk.

1645
01:28:25.370 --> 01:28:29.330
I mean, maybe no judgment, but I'm just saying, I don't know.

1646
01:28:29.590 --> 01:28:30.210
I judge.

1647
01:28:30.430 --> 01:28:31.130
Okay, go on.

1648
01:28:31.690 --> 01:28:32.650
We're at a restaurant.

1649
01:28:32.870 --> 01:28:34.230
Orders a tall glass of milk.

1650
01:28:35.070 --> 01:28:48.610
But he had this thing where he would take a bite of food and then immediately take a sip of milk and then chew the food with the milk in his mouth and then swallow it.

1651
01:28:48.630 --> 01:28:50.350
Oh, God.

1652
01:28:50.530 --> 01:28:54.170
And you had to sit and watch that through a whole meal?

1653
01:28:54.170 --> 01:28:58.250
Well, this was his preferred way of eating.

1654
01:28:58.530 --> 01:29:03.230
He liked the taste of his food mixed with a sip of milk.

1655
01:29:03.610 --> 01:29:04.950
All foods?

1656
01:29:05.810 --> 01:29:08.230
That's every meal, every food.

1657
01:29:08.410 --> 01:29:10.130
A bite of sandwich, sip of milk.

1658
01:29:10.610 --> 01:29:12.750
A fork full of spaghetti, sip of milk.

1659
01:29:12.970 --> 01:29:14.250
That is disgusting.

1660
01:29:15.390 --> 01:29:16.850
That's a deal breaker for me.

1661
01:29:16.950 --> 01:29:23.410
I can't spend the rest of my life watching you take one bite, a swig of milk, and slosh it around.

1662
01:29:23.530 --> 01:29:24.150
I can't do it.

1663
01:29:24.210 --> 01:29:24.490
I'm out.

1664
01:29:24.790 --> 01:29:26.330
I dated him a long time.

1665
01:29:26.490 --> 01:29:27.210
How long?

1666
01:29:27.730 --> 01:29:28.790
I don't want to say.

1667
01:29:28.910 --> 01:29:29.490
Oh, no.

1668
01:29:30.370 --> 01:29:31.210
Oh, no.

1669
01:29:31.350 --> 01:29:32.470
But it was a lot of meals.

1670
01:29:32.730 --> 01:29:34.390
A lot of milk meals.

1671
01:29:34.830 --> 01:29:35.350
Yeah.

1672
01:29:35.770 --> 01:29:42.990
Well, listen, Michael is really offended that Jan has pointed out this quirk in front of the dinner party.

1673
01:29:43.450 --> 01:29:45.650
And she is so evil.

1674
01:29:45.650 --> 01:29:47.510
She goes, oops.

1675
01:29:48.070 --> 01:29:49.030
And that's it.

1676
01:29:49.190 --> 01:29:50.190
Michael has had it.

1677
01:29:50.490 --> 01:29:52.970
He is going to take back his space.

1678
01:29:53.250 --> 01:29:54.630
He marches off.

1679
01:29:54.750 --> 01:29:56.690
We don't know where he's going or what he's getting.

1680
01:29:57.250 --> 01:30:01.290
While he's gone, I got a little glimpse of your plate, Angela.

1681
01:30:01.950 --> 01:30:02.310
Yeah?

1682
01:30:02.610 --> 01:30:04.830
Will you please tell people what you did?

1683
01:30:05.070 --> 01:30:07.930
You guys, it was one of those little actory moments.

1684
01:30:07.930 --> 01:30:13.130
And it might also have been because I was really pregnant and everything was smelling so strong to me.

1685
01:30:13.290 --> 01:30:18.250
But I took my napkin, my fancy napkin that Jan had laid out for all of us,

1686
01:30:18.350 --> 01:30:23.330
and I just gently covered my meat with it so I didn't have to look at it.

1687
01:30:23.530 --> 01:30:26.750
And I thought Angela Martin would do that because she's a vegetarian.

1688
01:30:26.750 --> 01:30:29.590
She wouldn't have eaten the meat or wanted to look at it.

1689
01:30:29.690 --> 01:30:35.610
But she wasn't going to say anything because this is clearly not the dinner party where you want to voice up about the food.

1690
01:30:35.970 --> 01:30:38.410
So I covered my meat with the napkin.

1691
01:30:38.690 --> 01:30:39.450
So brilliant.

1692
01:30:39.850 --> 01:30:40.890
I love that choice.

1693
01:30:41.470 --> 01:30:47.950
Well, Michael comes back to the table and he has brought with him his neon beer sign.

1694
01:30:47.950 --> 01:30:52.370
And he takes a painting off the wall, which, by the way, I want to point out is red.

1695
01:30:52.610 --> 01:30:53.050
Mm-hmm.

1696
01:30:53.270 --> 01:30:55.110
And he hangs up his beer sign.

1697
01:30:55.390 --> 01:30:59.210
And when the neon light goes on, you hear the hum.

1698
01:30:59.210 --> 01:31:04.190
And we are just bathed in this glow from this sign.

1699
01:31:04.390 --> 01:31:10.330
Well, listen, it's a St. Polly girl beer sign, and it's outlined in blue.

1700
01:31:10.610 --> 01:31:17.150
So when he turned it on, it was like a cascade of blue light filled the whole room.

1701
01:31:17.390 --> 01:31:18.830
It's just so incredible.

1702
01:31:18.830 --> 01:31:21.850
And you see the blue on Melora's face.

1703
01:31:22.050 --> 01:31:23.730
That's how bright the light is.

1704
01:31:24.490 --> 01:31:26.470
Jan is furious.

1705
01:31:27.230 --> 01:31:28.250
She gets up.

1706
01:31:28.370 --> 01:31:30.270
She turns on Hunter's CD.

1707
01:31:30.570 --> 01:31:34.070
And now we are going to have the argument.

1708
01:31:34.550 --> 01:31:35.070
Yeah.

1709
01:31:35.250 --> 01:31:39.290
We thought we had the argument, but now the showdown is about to happen.

1710
01:31:39.590 --> 01:31:40.190
Yeah.

1711
01:31:40.190 --> 01:31:45.050
They start arguing about talent, about creativity.

1712
01:31:45.870 --> 01:31:48.670
Michael's like, I don't think he's a good singer.

1713
01:31:48.670 --> 01:31:50.530
I don't think he's very good at all.

1714
01:31:50.630 --> 01:31:52.330
But Jan seems to love him.

1715
01:31:52.490 --> 01:31:54.790
It's one of my favorite lines.

1716
01:31:55.290 --> 01:31:57.470
Jan says, at least he's an artiSt.

1717
01:31:57.710 --> 01:32:01.090
And Michael says, BFD, I'm a screenwriter.

1718
01:32:01.330 --> 01:32:03.410
And this is my favorite line.

1719
01:32:03.770 --> 01:32:08.890
Jan says, and I'm a candle maker, but you don't hear me bragging about it.

1720
01:32:09.570 --> 01:32:12.510
Yeah, it's one of my favorite lines of the whole episode.

1721
01:32:13.370 --> 01:32:15.050
I also like this couplet.

1722
01:32:15.370 --> 01:32:17.770
You burn it, you buy it.

1723
01:32:17.950 --> 01:32:21.830
And then Michael says, great, I'll be your first customer.

1724
01:32:22.090 --> 01:32:24.150
You're hardly my firSt.

1725
01:32:29.330 --> 01:32:31.850
Leave, we got to sit in that room.

1726
01:32:32.210 --> 01:32:32.930
I know.

1727
01:32:33.230 --> 01:32:38.310
I mean, we got front row seats to this live show.

1728
01:32:38.670 --> 01:32:40.570
It was mind blowing.

1729
01:32:40.570 --> 01:32:47.250
Just the two of them were doing this dance and we got to watch it.

1730
01:32:47.370 --> 01:32:50.170
I am still blown away that we got to be there.

1731
01:32:50.450 --> 01:32:55.750
Well, when we asked Rainn Wilson about this episode, this is what he talked about.

1732
01:32:55.750 --> 01:33:08.590
I think the true hero of Dinner Party is the magnificent Melora Hardin, who is insanely brilliant all through the series, but especially in that episode.

1733
01:33:08.590 --> 01:33:22.030
I mean, Steve Carell being one of the all-time greats on the planet Earth comedic actors, and Melora Hardin stands toe-to-toe with him all the way through it, being just as funny,

1734
01:33:22.230 --> 01:33:24.510
just as specific, just as weird.

1735
01:33:24.510 --> 01:33:37.570
And it's where you kind of see that Jan has turned a corner and that there is underneath this kind of external facade of blonde efficiency.

1736
01:33:37.570 --> 01:33:43.770
There is a very, very weird, egotistical, messed up human being under there.

1737
01:33:43.990 --> 01:33:45.930
Her candles, on and on.

1738
01:33:46.110 --> 01:33:48.670
But her performance is just magnificent.

1739
01:33:48.690 --> 01:33:50.030
It's so dry.

1740
01:33:50.370 --> 01:33:59.810
It stands the test of time as just one of the great all-time performances all throughout the series, but especially in that episode.

1741
01:33:59.990 --> 01:34:05.370
When I rewatched it recently with my son, I was blown away by how great she was.

1742
01:34:06.610 --> 01:34:08.690
Melora is the star of this episode.

1743
01:34:08.890 --> 01:34:09.890
She just is.

1744
01:34:10.370 --> 01:34:10.670
Yeah.

1745
01:34:11.070 --> 01:34:13.350
We were so lucky to have her.

1746
01:34:13.570 --> 01:34:19.410
I mean, back on the pilot when we cast her, could we have known that this is what was going to happen?

1747
01:34:19.870 --> 01:34:29.290
Well, Jenna, Melora has shared with us that she felt like they knew the chemistry these characters could have if they really got room to run.

1748
01:34:29.490 --> 01:34:31.990
Way back on the pilot, here's what she had to say.

1749
01:34:31.990 --> 01:34:39.110
The whole Jan and Michael arc started when we were having lunch at the pilot episode.

1750
01:34:39.530 --> 01:34:43.270
Me and Steve and Greg were all having lunch together.

1751
01:34:43.530 --> 01:34:53.610
And somehow Steve and I both said, like, there was just some spark and some weird dysfunctional attraction between Michael and Jan that if we ever got so lucky to make the series,

1752
01:34:53.610 --> 01:34:58.330
we would hope that we could get them to hook up somehow, some way at some conference or something.

1753
01:34:58.490 --> 01:34:59.890
So that was the beginning of it.

1754
01:34:59.890 --> 01:35:12.950
So I think going into it, I was always aware of what the potential for sort of showing this wonderfully complicated and dysfunctional relationship was the hilarity of that.

1755
01:35:13.090 --> 01:35:21.370
It was just so funny and so kind of dark, darkly funny, which just really appeals to my personal sensibilities.

1756
01:35:21.370 --> 01:35:28.110
I really loved that the dinner party took it to that next step of implosion.

1757
01:35:28.550 --> 01:35:29.650
Yeah, I was just thrilled.

1758
01:35:29.830 --> 01:35:39.790
I was just thrilled that we had a chance to really implode on screen in front of everybody and hopefully get a lot of laughs out of it, which we did.

1759
01:35:39.790 --> 01:35:55.630
Well, speaking of implosion, this whole thing is about to crescendo when Jan picks up a Dundee and smashes Michael's beloved plasma screen TV.

1760
01:35:56.830 --> 01:36:06.380
Yeah, I mean, he's like, back on your zero dollar salary, babe.

1761
01:36:07.640 --> 01:36:13.860
Oh, my favorite moment after that, there's the silence of like, oh, my God, what just happened?

1762
01:36:13.860 --> 01:36:20.140
And the person that calls it for the night that's like, yeah, I'm done here is Melvina.

1763
01:36:20.560 --> 01:36:22.440
She's like, yeah, I'm going to go.

1764
01:36:23.460 --> 01:36:26.700
Well, Melvina is the only person who doesn't work for this guy.

1765
01:36:26.780 --> 01:36:30.480
So she could be like, yeah, I'm out of here.

1766
01:36:30.780 --> 01:36:30.920
Yeah.

1767
01:36:31.180 --> 01:36:32.740
This has taken a turn for me.

1768
01:36:32.740 --> 01:36:37.520
Well, we had a fan question, Angela, from Meg, Emily, Ethan and Emma.

1769
01:36:37.800 --> 01:36:45.180
How many plasma screen TVs were broken by a Dundee and how many takes did this actually require?

1770
01:36:45.480 --> 01:36:52.220
Well, I reached out to good old Kentopedia, who told me that those little TVs were actually kind of expensive.

1771
01:36:52.800 --> 01:36:57.620
He said they bought five of them and we broke four.

1772
01:36:58.000 --> 01:37:02.640
Oh, now I remember doing a bunch of takes with Melora where she missed.

1773
01:37:02.740 --> 01:37:06.480
At first, and they would have us react as if she hit it.

1774
01:37:06.720 --> 01:37:09.020
They could always use our reaction.

1775
01:37:09.560 --> 01:37:16.260
But then she only had those five chances to actually land the Dundee when she was on camera.

1776
01:37:16.520 --> 01:37:21.000
And, you know, I mean, the sort of comical thing is it wasn't a big target.

1777
01:37:21.720 --> 01:37:26.420
It's a small thing to hit square in the middle with a Dundee.

1778
01:37:26.720 --> 01:37:27.480
It's true.

1779
01:37:27.860 --> 01:37:30.860
Well, we're all going to follow Melvina out the door, right?

1780
01:37:30.860 --> 01:37:32.400
Everyone gets up from the table.

1781
01:37:32.760 --> 01:37:33.460
They're going to leave.

1782
01:37:33.660 --> 01:37:37.060
I was actually asked not to get up from the table, if you notice.

1783
01:37:37.620 --> 01:37:39.380
And it's because you would have seen my belly.

1784
01:37:39.540 --> 01:37:42.780
So I'm the last to leave the dining room.

1785
01:37:42.960 --> 01:37:46.000
Well, not only do we leave, but the police arrive.

1786
01:37:46.400 --> 01:37:49.340
There are two moments that are so delicious in the scene.

1787
01:37:49.660 --> 01:37:52.900
Well, one of my first things is right away the police officers are like,

1788
01:37:53.000 --> 01:37:55.920
hey, Dwight, because they know him because he's always hanging around them.

1789
01:37:55.920 --> 01:37:57.520
He, like, wants to be part of the club.

1790
01:37:58.120 --> 01:38:04.580
And the other thing is, is when Michael says to them, as if they know what he's talking about,

1791
01:38:04.660 --> 01:38:08.300
he says, my girlfriend threw a Dundee at my TV.

1792
01:38:08.940 --> 01:38:09.480
Yeah.

1793
01:38:09.900 --> 01:38:10.800
Can you imagine?

1794
01:38:12.830 --> 01:38:18.030
Well, they ask if he wants to press charges because some neighbors heard a lot of yelling,

1795
01:38:18.270 --> 01:38:19.650
a big domestic disturbance.

1796
01:38:20.150 --> 01:38:23.030
And Michael says, I'll take the fall.

1797
01:38:23.230 --> 01:38:28.370
And they're like, no, I, there's, you're actually, you're actually not in fault.

1798
01:38:28.590 --> 01:38:30.190
You don't have to take the fall.

1799
01:38:30.470 --> 01:38:32.490
Is there anywhere you can go tonight?

1800
01:38:32.870 --> 01:38:33.250
Yeah.

1801
01:38:33.250 --> 01:38:36.770
And Dwight offers to take Michael home with him,

1802
01:38:37.010 --> 01:38:41.390
which Michael refuses until he sees Jan come out of the condo.

1803
01:38:41.530 --> 01:38:42.630
And then he's like, yeah, yeah.

1804
01:38:42.730 --> 01:38:44.050
Okay, no, I'll go home with you.

1805
01:38:44.510 --> 01:38:49.110
Well, Jenna, as everyone is leaving, there was a Dwight and Angela deleted scene.

1806
01:38:49.590 --> 01:38:53.170
And Angela is very sassy with Dwight.

1807
01:38:53.550 --> 01:38:54.750
I want to play it.

1808
01:38:55.410 --> 01:38:57.570
I noticed you're wearing open-toed shoes.

1809
01:38:58.770 --> 01:39:00.310
Since when did you become a whore?

1810
01:39:01.590 --> 01:39:04.410
There might be a lot of things about me that shock you.

1811
01:39:05.830 --> 01:39:09.350
Now, if you excuse me, I have to get back to my date.

1812
01:39:11.230 --> 01:39:13.910
There might be a lot of things about me that shock you.

1813
01:39:14.350 --> 01:39:19.550
And then I look him up and down, and I coyly kind of smile, and I walk away.

1814
01:39:21.890 --> 01:39:25.910
And now there's this series of scenes, right, that kind of wrap up the episode.

1815
01:39:26.090 --> 01:39:27.790
There's a montage of Jan.

1816
01:39:28.130 --> 01:39:29.710
She's trying to fix the Dundee.

1817
01:39:30.120 --> 01:39:32.230
You can tell she's sad.

1818
01:39:32.530 --> 01:39:35.150
She knows this night went horrible.

1819
01:39:35.950 --> 01:39:39.810
Clearly knows this is a night they might not come back from, right?

1820
01:39:40.350 --> 01:39:40.830
Yeah.

1821
01:39:41.150 --> 01:39:44.030
You see Jim and Pam having this really cute scene.

1822
01:39:44.150 --> 01:39:45.190
They finally got food.

1823
01:39:45.370 --> 01:39:46.190
They're having a hamburger.

1824
01:39:46.810 --> 01:39:47.290
Yes.

1825
01:39:47.470 --> 01:39:50.650
We got a fan question about this from Reagan Colliner,

1826
01:39:50.690 --> 01:39:53.970
who wants to know what burger place did Jim and Pam eat at the end

1827
01:39:53.970 --> 01:39:55.510
because the burgers looked amazing.

1828
01:39:56.030 --> 01:39:58.070
I'll tell you what, the burgers were amazing.

1829
01:39:58.250 --> 01:40:02.310
I don't know if it was just because I'd spent four days saying I was hungry,

1830
01:40:02.310 --> 01:40:06.030
but when I got that burger, I'm really eating it in that scene.

1831
01:40:06.030 --> 01:40:07.190
I think you can tell.

1832
01:40:07.190 --> 01:40:10.250
I think you were happy to eat anything other than that granola bar.

1833
01:40:10.470 --> 01:40:11.710
I think I was.

1834
01:40:12.850 --> 01:40:18.710
Well, we filmed that scene at the Home Plate Burger joint,

1835
01:40:18.710 --> 01:40:21.770
and it was this little mom-and-pop hamburger stand,

1836
01:40:21.790 --> 01:40:24.110
which eventually, sadly, went out of business.

1837
01:40:24.110 --> 01:40:25.550
It's now a smog shop.

1838
01:40:25.750 --> 01:40:28.330
And in that same strip mall,

1839
01:40:28.510 --> 01:40:33.910
there was a car wash that they turned into a Cold Stone Creamery,

1840
01:40:33.910 --> 01:40:39.190
and that is where Andy and Angela are sitting in the car having their ice cream.

1841
01:40:39.190 --> 01:40:40.030
Yes.

1842
01:40:40.450 --> 01:40:43.110
Ed and I have a very funny story about this moment.

1843
01:40:43.110 --> 01:40:44.390
And I asked Ed.

1844
01:40:44.490 --> 01:40:45.130
I texted him.

1845
01:40:45.250 --> 01:40:48.450
I said, Ed, can I share about the car scene?

1846
01:40:48.630 --> 01:40:53.010
And he's like, yes, you can tell everyone I farted in the car.

1847
01:40:53.990 --> 01:40:57.390
So we're in the car, and he's supposed to lick a little bit of my ice cream,

1848
01:40:57.390 --> 01:40:59.830
and then I have to squish it on the side, right?

1849
01:41:00.070 --> 01:41:03.490
It took a few tries to get that squish just right.

1850
01:41:03.850 --> 01:41:06.530
And in between setting up, they'd have to clean the door,

1851
01:41:06.690 --> 01:41:10.270
and we're in between setups, and Ed had a little toot.

1852
01:41:11.210 --> 01:41:15.490
I was really pregnant, as you guys know, and it smelled.

1853
01:41:15.730 --> 01:41:17.290
And I was like, oh, no, oh, no.

1854
01:41:17.910 --> 01:41:20.210
And we were rolling when it happened.

1855
01:41:20.370 --> 01:41:22.750
And so it's in the bloopers.

1856
01:41:23.550 --> 01:41:24.530
Here it is.

1857
01:41:25.790 --> 01:41:26.810
Oh, God.

1858
01:41:27.650 --> 01:41:28.590
Oh, God.

1859
01:41:29.370 --> 01:41:30.330
Oh, no.

1860
01:41:30.850 --> 01:41:33.090
If Angela's coming out of the car, I think I know what it is.

1861
01:41:33.450 --> 01:41:34.410
I'm sorry.

1862
01:41:45.600 --> 01:41:47.700
He drove you from the car.

1863
01:41:47.900 --> 01:41:48.760
You had to get out.

1864
01:41:48.820 --> 01:41:50.360
I had to get out of the car.

1865
01:41:50.660 --> 01:41:54.700
And our crew was listening the whole time, and they were cracking up.

1866
01:41:54.840 --> 01:41:57.480
Ed is hitting the dashboard like, no, no.

1867
01:41:59.340 --> 01:42:01.220
It cracks us up.

1868
01:42:01.320 --> 01:42:02.500
It makes me laugh.

1869
01:42:02.700 --> 01:42:03.380
Oh, my gosh.

1870
01:42:03.940 --> 01:42:09.900
Years later, Jenna, when the show wrapped, Ed gave me the sweetest card.

1871
01:42:10.140 --> 01:42:13.820
He wrote all of these lovely things, and he ended it with,

1872
01:42:13.820 --> 01:42:17.300
And I farted in a car with you, so we'll always have that.

1873
01:42:17.560 --> 01:42:18.420
Love Ed.

1874
01:42:23.260 --> 01:42:24.280
It happens.

1875
01:42:24.480 --> 01:42:26.440
But that one made the blooper real.

1876
01:42:28.140 --> 01:42:36.460
Well, the very last scene is Dwight and Michael pulling up to this bus stop, and as they pass

1877
01:42:36.460 --> 01:42:43.200
by, we can see that Dwight's babysitter is waiting for the bus with her cooler, and they

1878
01:42:43.200 --> 01:42:45.500
do not offer her a ride.

1879
01:42:46.080 --> 01:42:46.980
It's terrible.

1880
01:42:47.460 --> 01:42:52.540
But Beth Grant sent in a little memory of shooting this as well.

1881
01:42:52.760 --> 01:42:58.060
I must say, at the end, when I'm standing at the bus stop, waiting for the bus, because

1882
01:42:58.060 --> 01:43:02.740
he hasn't even had the decency to drive me home, and his car pulls up, and we have this

1883
01:43:02.740 --> 01:43:09.660
moment of looking at each other, to me, is so esoteric and brilliant and wonderful.

1884
01:43:09.660 --> 01:43:14.260
And Raines looked to me, and then he drives off, leaving me at the bus stop.

1885
01:43:15.380 --> 01:43:16.660
He's a free man.

1886
01:43:17.320 --> 01:43:22.160
I just love how tickled she is by her whole storyline in this.

1887
01:43:22.300 --> 01:43:25.820
She was so game for all of it, and I loved having her on set.

1888
01:43:25.960 --> 01:43:27.080
She was an absolute delight.

1889
01:43:27.820 --> 01:43:32.460
Yes, and Beth, oh my goodness, thank you so much for sending in these audio clips, and

1890
01:43:32.460 --> 01:43:38.860
thank you to Melora, and Rain, and John, and Ed, and Paul Feig, Gene, and Lee,

1891
01:43:38.860 --> 01:43:45.580
Kintopedia, Jenna, everyone really showed up for us for this episode, and Steve read the

1892
01:43:45.580 --> 01:43:46.100
summary.

1893
01:43:46.500 --> 01:43:49.500
Guys, that's dinner party.

1894
01:43:49.800 --> 01:43:51.380
We hope you liked it.

1895
01:43:51.720 --> 01:43:57.880
Angela and I worked extra long on this episode because we wanted to get everything we could

1896
01:43:57.880 --> 01:43:59.120
and share it with you.

1897
01:43:59.420 --> 01:44:04.300
This is one of our favorite memories of shooting the show, and we hope we did it justice.

1898
01:44:04.780 --> 01:44:06.580
We love you guys so much.

1899
01:44:06.740 --> 01:44:07.660
Thanks for listening.

1900
01:44:07.660 --> 01:44:09.560
Go light your candles.

1901
01:44:10.140 --> 01:44:13.820
Take a minute for yourself and find some serenity.

1902
01:44:14.360 --> 01:44:18.460
Sam, will you take us out with just one night?

1903
01:44:19.640 --> 01:44:48.400
Thank you for listening to Office Ladies' Second Drink.

1904
